# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bullet Heaven
#
# The game is plain static files with no build step, so there is almost nothing
# generated to ignore. This is mostly about keeping editor config and OS
# droppings out of a repo that is meant to be read.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored, because they are part of the project:
#   serve.py              the dev server. `python -m http.server` sends no cache
#                         headers and silently serves stale ES modules, which
#                         cost real debugging time, so the no-store server ships.
#   tools/                the balance benches the README documents.
#   test/                 the rune and spawn suites. `npm test` runs them.
#   docs/                 the design spec.
#   .claude/launch.json   encodes "serve.py on port 5174" -- the documented way
#                         to run this, useful to anyone who clones it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Python bytecode, from serve.py
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Node. package.json exists only to carry the `npm test` scripts -- there are no
# dependencies, so node_modules should never appear. Ignored in case it does.
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Claude Code: keep launch.json above, drop anything machine-specific
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.json

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Scratch
*.log
tmp/
scratch/
